@startuml 10_overview_simple
!include _style.iuml

title GPIO overview: the five boxes you need to understand first

left to right direction

rectangle "1. Application\n(your LED / relay / button logic)" as app #E3F2E1
rectangle "2. Pin\nknows only: which port, which bit\nNO state, NO lock" as pin #E3F2E1
rectangle "3. Port\none GPIO controller\nOWNS all pin state + the lock" as port #FFF4D6
rectangle "4. I2C / SPI module (same hal package)\nIRegisterDevice: moves register bytes\nbus controller OWNS the bus lock\n(details: diagram 11)" as bus #EAF1FB
rectangle "5. Hardware\nSoC GPIO registers\nor expander chip" as hw #F3E8FD
rectangle "OSAL\nmutex, ISR detection, event signal\n(one implementation per OS)" as osal #FDECE3

app --> pin : led.set(High)
pin --> port : write bit 3 = 1
port --> hw : native: 1 register store
port --> bus : expander: send bytes
bus --> hw : I2C / SPI transfer

port ..> osal : uses
bus ..> osal : uses

note bottom of port
  Rule 1: all mutable state lives here, in exactly one place.
  Rule 2: Port lock is always taken BEFORE Bus lock.
end note
@enduml
